A note on authentication and non-commercial use
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project's own code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
above, and may be freely used, modified, and redistributed — including
commercially — under the terms of that license.

Separately, and NOT covered by the Apache License grant: this project's
default authentication path reuses the credential of a Claude Code CLI
already installed and authenticated on the user's own machine, passed to
the Claude Agent SDK's child process via CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, instead
of requiring a separately configured Anthropic API key.

The Claude Agent SDK's own terms state:

  "Unless previously approved, Anthropic does not allow third party
  developers to offer claude.ai login or rate limits for their products,
  including agents built on the Claude Agent SDK."
  — Agent SDK Quickstart, https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/quickstart

For this specific project, Thariq at Anthropic clarified informally that
reusing a user's own local Claude Code CLI login in this way is acceptable
because this project is not commercialized.

That clarification:

  - was given to this project specifically, not as a general policy;
  - is conditioned on the project remaining non-commercial (no paid
    license, no "pro" tier, no product-linked sponsorship, no other form
    of monetization);
  - is not a license grant, is not transferable, and is NOT inherited by
    forks — including forks that keep this NOTICE and otherwise comply
    with the Apache License in every respect.

Anyone who forks this project and intends to commercialize it in any form
must either (a) obtain their own authorization from Anthropic before
relying on this authentication path, or (b) remove it and require users
to supply their own Anthropic API key (or another Anthropic-documented
authentication method) instead.

See docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #4 (Autenticação) in this repository for the
full context and the record of this decision.
